+## Skeleton injection
+
+`--nui_skeleton_inject=test` replaces every skeleton the title's own tracker
+fits with one xenia supplies, so that a skeleton from another tracker can
+drive the title. The only source so far, `test`, is a synthetic figure 2.2 m
+from the sensor that sways 0.35 m to either side over six seconds and jumps
+0.25 m every four; it is not anyone's pose. With the flag empty, the default,
+nothing below happens.
+
+**Where.** After the runtime's frame producer has filled a skeleton frame and
+before it publishes it, the producer calls a six-instruction thunk that calls
+through a function pointer in the runtime's state block when that pointer is
+set: `lis; lwz; cmplwi; beqlr; mtctr; bctr`. xenia finds
+`NuiSkeletonGetNextFrame` by the signature PS5X360 uses for it (a 0xAB0-byte
+copy, a wait clamped to 8000 ms, a conversion to 100 ns units and
+`0x8007048F`), reads the state block, the slot ring and the frame's offset in a
+slot out of its instructions, and then looks for that thunk, calling through a
+pointer inside the state block. Each step must find exactly one match, and the
+thunk exactly one caller. The thunk is bound to the host the way xenia binds an
+import (`sc 2; blr` and an extern handler) when the title registers its
+runtime with message 0x2B003, before the camera worker runs. The handler
+rewrites the frame's six skeleton slots, keeping each slot's enrollment index
+and user index words, which the runtime's identity pass writes. It then calls
+the runtime's own callback when the pointer is set; the pointer was null in
+every run so far. The frame's header is left as the runtime wrote it: timestamp, frame number, flags,
+floor plane and gravity. So `NuiSkeletonGetNextFrame`, the HUD message 0x2B002, the Kinect
+Guide and the play-frame log all see the injected skeleton.
+
+```
+NUI: skeleton injection (source "test"): NuiSkeletonGetNextFrame at 82D26768, runtime state at 83896510, frame slots at +A70 every AE0 with the frame at +20, frame callback thunk at 82D263C0 (pointer at 83898DFC) called from 82D222C8, now bound to the host.
+NUI: skeleton injection frame 900 (runtime frame 1638): replaced tracker slots [0:1/402/-1/254 1:1/403/-1/254 2:0/0/-1/254 3:0/0/-1/254 4:0/0/-1/254 5:0/0/-1/254]
+```
+
+The addresses are from a different disc revision of `4D5308ED` (module hash
+`FC152DDFE29E856E`) than the rest of this document. The second line repeats
+about every 900 frames. It lists what the tracker had put in each slot, as
+`slot:state/id/enrollment index/user index`. Any step that fails is logged at
+Warning, and the title keeps its own tracker's skeletons.
+
+**What still comes from the depth path.** The producer runs once per depth
+frame, so depth frames must keep flowing; they pace the skeleton frames. The
+floor plane is still the tracker's fit to the depth image. The player-index
+textures are still the tracker's segmentation, numbered by the tracker's own
+slots: with the test figure in slot 0, the mask held indices 5, 3 or 1 from
+frame to frame.
+
